  "content": {
    "id": "p8-q15-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "15",
    "prompt": "The expression\n$$(\\sqrt{70}+1)^{70}+(\\sqrt{70}-1)^{70}$$\nis an integer. Find its units digit.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "2.\n\nAdd the binomial expansions: odd powers of $\\sqrt{70}$ cancel, and every remaining nonconstant term is divisible by 10.",
      "worked": "Let $S=(\\sqrt{70}+1)^{70}+(\\sqrt{70}-1)^{70}$. In the two binomial expansions, terms containing odd powers of $\\sqrt{70}$ cancel and terms containing even powers add.\n$$\\begin{align*}S&=2\\sum_{j=0}^{35}\\binom{70}{2j}(\\sqrt{70})^{2j}\\\\S&=2\\sum_{j=0}^{35}\\binom{70}{2j}70^j\\\\S&=2+2\\sum_{j=1}^{35}\\binom{70}{2j}70^j.\\end{align*}$$\nEvery term in the final sum is an integer divisible by 10. Therefore $S$ has units digit 2.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 55
  },
